Subject: [PATCH 14/29] fix(emboss): re-freeze the 5-state shape182..glyph178
 milestone chain

test_shape182_is_exact_delta_over_emboss181_glitch180_edge179_and_glyph178
regenerates FIVE historical milestones (live182, emboss181, glitch180,
edge179, glyph178) and compares each one's spec-JSON hash plus its three
generated-artifact hashes to frozen values. All were stale under the
0ed489ec corpus bump for the same reason as the edge/glyph-map/task35
fixes: none of these five milestones' exclusion sets remove the 9-10
corpus-bump-changed programs (filter/adjust, filter/chrome:chMap,
filter/grade x2, filter/invert:inv, filter/text:text,
filter/tint:colorize, mixer/alphaMask, mixer/blendMode,
synth/media:mediaInput), so they ride into every one of the five
projections.

The test's own assertions are not subTest-wrapped for the spec-hash
check, so only the FIRST state's (live182) mismatch was visible in any
prior run -- the other four states' drift was hidden behind it. Wrote a
standalone script (mirrors the test's exact projection-building code) to
compute all 5 spec hashes and all 15 artifact hashes in one process,
rather than whack-a-mole re-running this ~7-minute test five times.

Cross-checked against independent evidence instead of trusting a single
source: the edge179 and glyph178 artifact hashes computed here are
byte-identical to the freshly-verified values in the just-fixed
test_edge_bvec3_contour.py and test_glyph_map_nonnegative_int_shift.py
(same milestones, same exclusion-set composition, computed by three
separate scripts/tests) -- three-way agreement. The live182 spec hash
also matches the one "actual" value the very first (pre-fix) shard run
printed for this test, which is a hash of program-list metadata only
(load_slice's slice.json shape), unaffected by the later scalar_uint_xor
manifest-generation shift that made edge_bvec3's original re-freeze
attempt wrong -- consistent with that shift being confined to
generate_outputs's typed_manifest.json rendering, not load_slice.

Re-pinned all 5 spec hashes and all 15 artifact hashes (5 states x
{typed_slice.cpp, typed_manifest.json, catalog.hpp}). Full module passes:
Ran 22 tests ... OK (skipped=7, all skips are authority-gated NOISEMAKER_CPU_ROOT/NOISEMAKER_FOR_CPU checks correctly absent in this env).

